IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- THE NOUNS of piece cr2 (regulations 37 to 78.4).
-- Layer 1. Declarations only: no rules, no #EVAL. Every other cr2 module imports this one.
--
-- What is here: the lists of information or evidence the Regulations require a person to set out, furnish or
-- supply (one enumeration per list, one constructor per paragraph), and the few other kinds of thing the Part
-- distinguishes (a way of applying, a kind of attendance at school, a payee).
-- Why enumerations: a rule can then ask which items are still owed, and a test can name them.
-- Naming: a type this piece coins is called `cr2 ...`; a constructor begins with the regulation and paragraph
-- that license it, so that it cannot clash with any other piece's names after the merge.
--
-- The type `Minister` of the core names the two Ministers; the Regulations' Part V reads "the Minister" as
-- the Minister of Employment and Social Development (regulation 2(1), piece cr1).

§ `Part V -- the nouns`

§§ `Regulation 39 -- the ways of applying for a statement of earnings`

-- src:431 | 39 (1) An application under subsection 96(1) of the Act by a contributor to require the Minister to inform the contributor of the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the contributor’s account in the Record of Earnings shall be made to the Minister in writing. The application may also be made to the Minister by way of the Internet on the electronic form prescribed for that purpose and made available on the Internet.
-- src:432 | (2) An application made in writing shall include the contributor’s name, address (including the postal code) and Social Insurance Number.
-- src:433 | (3) An application made by way of the Internet shall include the contributor’s name, Social Insurance Number and postal code.
@ref Reg 39 (src:431-433)
DECLARE `cr2 Way of applying for a statement of earnings` IS ONE OF
    `an application in writing to the Minister`
    `an application to the Minister by way of the Internet on the electronic form prescribed for that purpose`
    `an application made in some other way`

§§ `Regulation 46(2) -- what a notification of a division must contain`

-- src:459 | (2) A notification required by subsection 55(8) or 55.2(10) of the Act shall be effected by giving notice in writing containing such of the following information as is applicable:
-- src:460 | (a) the dates of marriage and dissolution of marriage of the persons subject to the division;
-- src:461 | (b) the period of cohabitation for which the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings has been made;
-- src:462 | (c) the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings, prior to the division, of the persons subject to the division;
-- src:463 | (d) the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons subject to the division as a result of the division;
-- src:464 | (e) the effect of the division on any benefit that is payable to or in respect of the persons subject to the division;
-- src:465 | (f) a statement of the right to make a request for a reconsideration referred to in subsection 81(1) of the Act; and
-- src:466 | (g) any other information that the Minister deems necessary.
@ref Reg 46(2) (src:459-466)
DECLARE `cr2 Item of the notice of a division` IS ONE OF
    `reg 46(2)(a) — the dates of marriage and dissolution of marriage of the persons subject to the division`
    `reg 46(2)(b) — the period of cohabitation for which the division has been made`
    `reg 46(2)(c) — the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons before the division`
    `reg 46(2)(d) — the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons as a result of the division`
    `reg 46(2)(e) — the effect of the division on any benefit payable to or in respect of the persons`
    `reg 46(2)(f) — a statement of the right to make a request for a reconsideration referred to in subsection 81(1) of the Act`
    `reg 46(2)(g) — any other information that the Minister deems necessary`

§§ `Regulation 52 -- information and evidence an applicant or beneficiary must set out or furnish`

-- src:500 | 52 For the purposes of determining the eligibility of an applicant for a benefit, the amount that an applicant or beneficiary is entitled to receive as a benefit or the eligibility of a beneficiary to continue to receive a benefit, the applicant, the person applying on his behalf, or the beneficiary, as the case may be, shall, in the application, or thereafter in writing when requested to do so by the Minister, set out or furnish the Minister with the following applicable information or evidence:
-- src:501 | (a) the name at birth and present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of
-- src:502 | (i) the applicant or beneficiary,
-- src:503 | (ii) the disabled or deceased contributor,
-- src:504 | (iii) the spouse or common-law partner of the disabled contributor or the survivor of the deceased contributor,
-- src:505 | (iv) each dependent child of the disabled or deceased contributor, and
-- src:506 | (v) any former spouse or former common-law partner, where known to the applicant;
-- src:507 | (b) the date and place of birth of
-- src:508 | (i) the applicant or beneficiary,
-- src:509 | (ii) the disabled or deceased contributor,
-- src:510 | (iii) the survivor of the deceased contributor, and
-- src:511 | (iv) each dependent child of the disabled or deceased contributor;
-- src:512 | (c) the date and place of death of the contributor;
-- src:513 | (d) whether a dependent child of the contributor has died since
-- src:514 | (i) the date on which the contributor claims to have become disabled, or
-- src:515 | (ii) the death of the contributor;
-- src:516 | (e) [Repealed, SOR/86-1133, s. 10]
-- src:517 | (f) whether the deceased contributor was married at the time of his death and, if so, to whom, and the date and place of the marriage;
-- src:518 | (g) whether the deceased contributor was separated or divorced at the time of his death;
-- src:519 | (h) whether there is a personal representative of the estate of the deceased contributor, and the name and address of any such personal representative;
-- src:520 | (i) whether a dependent child of the disabled or deceased contributor
-- src:521 | (i) is his child,
-- src:522 | (ii) is his legally adopted child or was adopted in fact by him or is a legally adopted child of another person,
-- src:523 | (iii) was a child, in respect of whom, either legally or in fact, the contributor had parenting time or decision-making responsibility,
-- src:524 | (iv) is a child, in respect of whom, the disabled contributor, the survivor of the contributor or another person or agency had decision-making responsibility,
-- src:525 | (v) [Repealed, SOR/2024-265, s. 3]
-- src:526 | (vi) is or was maintained by the disabled contributor;
-- src:527 | (j) if a dependent child of the disabled or deceased contributor is 18 or more years of age, whether that child is or was in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university;
-- src:528 | (k) whether the applicant or beneficiary who is the survivor of a contributor maintains wholly or substantially one or more dependent children of the deceased contributor;
-- src:529 | (k.1) [Repealed, SOR/2013-83, s. 2]
-- src:530 | (l) a statement evidencing the amount of the contributory salary and wages and of the contributory self-employed earnings of a disabled or deceased contributor for the year in which the contributor became disabled or died and for any preceding year;
-- src:531 | (m) whether the applicant, beneficiary or deceased contributor is or was in receipt of or has applied for a benefit under the Act or under a provincial pension plan or a pension under the Old Age Security Act; and
-- src:532 | (n) such additional documents, statements or records that are in the possession of the applicant or beneficiary or are obtainable by him that will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information and evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) to (m).
@ref Reg 52 (src:500-532)
DECLARE `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 52` IS ONE OF
    `reg 52(a)(i) — the name at birth, present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of the applicant or beneficiary`
    `reg 52(a)(ii) — the name at birth, present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of the disabled or deceased contributor`
    `reg 52(a)(iii) — the name at birth, present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of the spouse or common-law partner of the disabled contributor or the survivor of the deceased contributor`
    `reg 52(a)(iv) — the name at birth, present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of each dependent child of the disabled or deceased contributor`
    `reg 52(a)(v) — the name at birth, present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of any former spouse or former common-law partner, where known to the applicant`
    `reg 52(b)(i) — the date and place of birth of the applicant or beneficiary`
    `reg 52(b)(ii) — the date and place of birth of the disabled or deceased contributor`
    `reg 52(b)(iii) — the date and place of birth of the survivor of the deceased contributor`
    `reg 52(b)(iv) — the date and place of birth of each dependent child of the disabled or deceased contributor`
    `reg 52(c) — the date and place of death of the contributor`
    `reg 52(d)(i) — whether a dependent child of the contributor has died since the date on which the contributor claims to have become disabled`
    `reg 52(d)(ii) — whether a dependent child of the contributor has died since the death of the contributor`
    `reg 52(f) — whether the deceased contributor was married at the time of death and, if so, to whom, and the date and place of the marriage`
    `reg 52(g) — whether the deceased contributor was separated or divorced at the time of death`
    `reg 52(h) — whether there is a personal representative of the estate of the deceased contributor, and the name and address of any such personal representative`
    `reg 52(i)(i) — whether a dependent child of the disabled or deceased contributor is the contributor's child`
    `reg 52(i)(ii) — whether such a child is the contributor's legally adopted child, was adopted in fact by the contributor, or is a legally adopted child of another person`
    `reg 52(i)(iii) — whether such a child was a child in respect of whom the contributor had parenting time or decision-making responsibility`
    `reg 52(i)(iv) — whether such a child is a child in respect of whom the disabled contributor, the survivor or another person or agency had decision-making responsibility`
    `reg 52(i)(vi) — whether such a child is or was maintained by the disabled contributor`
    `reg 52(j) — whether a dependent child aged 18 or more of the disabled or deceased contributor is or was in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university`
    `reg 52(k) — whether the applicant or beneficiary who is the survivor of a contributor maintains wholly or substantially one or more dependent children of the deceased contributor`
    `reg 52(l) — a statement evidencing the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings of the disabled or deceased contributor`
    `reg 52(m) — whether the applicant, beneficiary or deceased contributor is or was in receipt of, or has applied for, a benefit under the Act or a provincial pension plan or a pension under the Old Age Security Act`
    `reg 52(n) — such additional documents, statements or records as will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information and evidence in paragraphs (a) to (m)`

§§ `Regulation 53 -- additional information on family allowance months`

-- src:533 | 53 For the purposes of determining whether any months during which a contributor was a family allowance recipient should not be included in his contributory period, the applicant shall, in the application or thereafter in writing when requested to do so by the Minister, set out or furnish the Minister with such of the following additional information or evidence as is applicable:
-- src:534 | (a) the name and date of birth of all children in respect of whom the contributor received family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits;
-- src:535 | (b) the Social Insurance Number, if any, of each of those children;
-- src:536 | (c) the periods during which the contributor received family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits in respect of those children;
-- src:537 | (d) the province in which the contributor resided while in receipt of family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits in respect of those children;
-- src:538 | (e) the Social Insurance Number of the contributor to whom family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits were paid in respect of those children;
-- src:539 | (f) if known, the name and Social Insurance Number of any other person who received family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits in respect of those children; and
-- src:540 | (g) such additional documents, statements or records that are in the possession of the applicant or are obtainable by him that will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information and evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) to (f).
@ref Reg 53 (src:533-540)
DECLARE `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 53` IS ONE OF
    `reg 53(a) — the name and date of birth of all children for whom the contributor received family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits`
    `reg 53(b) — the Social Insurance Number, if any, of each of those children`
    `reg 53(c) — the periods during which the contributor received those benefits for those children`
    `reg 53(d) — the province in which the contributor resided while in receipt of those benefits`
    `reg 53(e) — the Social Insurance Number of the contributor to whom those benefits were paid`
    `reg 53(f) — if known, the name and Social Insurance Number of any other person who received those benefits for those children`
    `reg 53(g) — such additional documents, statements or records as will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information in paragraphs (a) to (f)`

§§ `Regulation 54(1) -- information for an application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings`

-- src:541 | 54 (1) For the purpose of determining whether an application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act may be approved, the applicant must, set out in the application, or furnish in writing when requested to do so by the Minister, the information required under section 52, with any modifications that the circumstances require, as well as the following information or evidence, as is applicable:
-- src:542 | (a) the name at birth and present name, the sex, address and Social Insurance Number of each spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner;
-- src:543 | (b) the date and place of birth of each spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner;
-- src:544 | (c) whether the spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner is or was in receipt of or has applied for a benefit under the Act or under a provincial pension plan;
-- src:545 | (d) the date and place of marriage of the spouses or former spouses and their certificate of marriage, a copy of that certificate or a copy of their act of marriage;
-- src:546 | (e) the date and place of the dissolution of the marriage of the former spouses;
-- src:547 | (f) documentary evidence of any such dissolution of marriage, including the decree absolute of divorce, the judgment granting a divorce under the Divorce Act, or the judgment of nullity;
-- src:548 | (g) the address of all residences where the spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners lived together;
-- src:549 | (h) the dates of any periods when the spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners did not live together and whether the separations or any of them were for any reason set out in paragraph 78(2)(a) or subsection 78.1(3);
-- src:550 | (i) the date that the spouses, former spouses or former common- law partners commenced to live separate and apart;
-- src:551 | (j) the dates of all periods when the spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners lived together in a conjugal relationship;
-- src:552 | (k) a copy of any written agreement between persons subject to a division that was entered into before June 4, 1986 or any written agreement between such persons that was entered into on or after that date and contains a provision that is binding on the Minister under subsection 55.2(3) of the Act; and
-- src:553 | (l) such additional documents, statements or records that are in the possession of, or are obtainable by, the applicant as will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information and evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) to (k).
@ref Reg 54(1) (src:541-553)
DECLARE `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 54(1)` IS ONE OF
    `reg 54(1) chapeau — the information required under regulation 52, with any modifications that the circumstances require`
    `reg 54(1)(a) — the name at birth, present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of each spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner`
    `reg 54(1)(b) — the date and place of birth of each spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner`
    `reg 54(1)(c) — whether each spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner is or was in receipt of, or has applied for, a benefit under the Act or a provincial pension plan`
    `reg 54(1)(d) — the date and place of marriage and the certificate of marriage, a copy of it or a copy of the act of marriage`
    `reg 54(1)(e) — the date and place of the dissolution of the marriage`
    `reg 54(1)(f) — documentary evidence of the dissolution of the marriage, including the decree absolute of divorce, the judgment granting a divorce under the Divorce Act, or the judgment of nullity`
    `reg 54(1)(g) — the address of all residences where the spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners lived together`
    `reg 54(1)(h) — the dates of any periods when they did not live together and whether the separations were for any reason set out in paragraph 78(2)(a) or subsection 78.1(3)`
    `reg 54(1)(i) — the date that they commenced to live separate and apart`
    `reg 54(1)(j) — the dates of all periods when they lived together in a conjugal relationship`
    `reg 54(1)(k) — a copy of any written agreement between the persons subject to a division that was made before June 4, 1986, or on or after that date and binds the Minister under subsection 55.2(3) of the Act`
    `reg 54(1)(l) — such additional documents, statements or records as will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information and evidence in paragraphs (a) to (k)`

§§ `Regulation 54(2) -- information relating to the marriage, for paragraph 55.1(1)(a) of the Act`

-- src:554 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph 55.1(1)(a) of the Act, the information relating to the marriage is the following, as is applicable:
-- src:555 | (a) the name at birth and present name, the sex, address and Social Insurance Number of each of the former spouses;
-- src:556 | (b) the date and place of marriage of the former spouses and their certificate of marriage, a copy of that certificate or a copy of their act of marriage;
-- src:557 | (c) the date and place of the dissolution of the marriage of the former spouses;
-- src:558 | (d) a copy of the decree or judgment referred to in that paragraph;
-- src:559 | (e) the addresses of all residences where the former spouses lived together;
-- src:560 | (f) the dates of any periods when the former spouses did not live together and whether the separations or any of them were for any reason set out in paragraph 78(2)(a) or subsection 78.1(3);
-- src:561 | (g) the date that the former spouses commenced to live separate and apart;
-- src:562 | (h) the dates of all periods when the former spouses lived together in a conjugal relationship; and
-- src:563 | (i) a copy of any written agreement between persons subject to a division that was entered into before June 4, 1986 or any written agreement between such persons that was entered into on or after that date and contains a provision that is binding on the Minister under subsection 55.2(3) of the Act.
@ref Reg 54(2) (src:554-563)
DECLARE `cr2 Item of information relating to the marriage under regulation 54(2)` IS ONE OF
    `reg 54(2)(a) — the name at birth, present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of each of the former spouses`
    `reg 54(2)(b) — the date and place of marriage and the certificate of marriage, a copy of it or a copy of the act of marriage`
    `reg 54(2)(c) — the date and place of the dissolution of the marriage`
    `reg 54(2)(d) — a copy of the decree or judgment referred to in paragraph 55.1(1)(a) of the Act`
    `reg 54(2)(e) — the addresses of all residences where the former spouses lived together`
    `reg 54(2)(f) — the dates of any periods when the former spouses did not live together and whether the separations were for any reason set out in paragraph 78(2)(a) or subsection 78.1(3)`
    `reg 54(2)(g) — the date that the former spouses commenced to live separate and apart`
    `reg 54(2)(h) — the dates of all periods when the former spouses lived together in a conjugal relationship`
    `reg 54(2)(i) — a copy of any written agreement between the persons subject to a division that was made before June 4, 1986, or on or after that date and binds the Minister under subsection 55.2(3) of the Act`

§§ `Regulation 54.1(1) -- information for an application for an assignment of a portion of a retirement pension`

-- src:565 | 54.1 (1) For the purpose of determining whether an application for an assignment of a portion of a retirement pension under section 65.1 of the Act may be approved, the applicant must set out in the application, or furnish in writing when requested to do so by the Minister, the information required under section 52, with any modifications that the circumstances require, as well as the following information or evidence, as is applicable:
-- src:566 | (a) the name at birth and present name, the sex, address and Social Insurance Number of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:567 | (b) the date and place of birth of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:568 | (c) whether the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner is or was in receipt of or has applied for a benefit under the Act or under a provincial pension plan;
-- src:569 | (d) the date and place of marriage of the spouses and their certificate of marriage, a copy of that certificate or a copy of their act of marriage;
-- src:570 | (e) the month in which the spouses or common-law partners commenced to live together in a conjugal relationship;
-- src:571 | (f) the dates of any periods when the spouses or common-law partners did not live together and whether the separations or any of them were for any reason set out in paragraph 78(2)(a) or subsection 78.1(3);
-- src:572 | (g) documentary evidence of the dissolution of any previous marriage of the applicant, including the decree absolute of divorce, the judgment granting a divorce under the Divorce Act or the judgment of nullity; and
-- src:573 | (h) such additional documents, statements or records that are in the possession of, or are obtainable by, the applicant as will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information and evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) to (g).
@ref Reg 54.1(1) (src:565-573)
DECLARE `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 54.1(1)` IS ONE OF
    `reg 54.1(1) chapeau — the information required under regulation 52, with any modifications that the circumstances require`
    `reg 54.1(1)(a) — the name at birth, present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of the applicant's spouse or common-law partner`
    `reg 54.1(1)(b) — the date and place of birth of the applicant's spouse or common-law partner`
    `reg 54.1(1)(c) — whether the applicant's spouse or common-law partner is or was in receipt of, or has applied for, a benefit under the Act or a provincial pension plan`
    `reg 54.1(1)(d) — the date and place of marriage and the certificate of marriage, a copy of it or a copy of the act of marriage`
    `reg 54.1(1)(e) — the month in which the spouses or common-law partners commenced to live together in a conjugal relationship`
    `reg 54.1(1)(f) — the dates of any periods when they did not live together and whether the separations were for any reason set out in paragraph 78(2)(a) or subsection 78.1(3)`
    `reg 54.1(1)(g) — documentary evidence of the dissolution of any previous marriage of the applicant`
    `reg 54.1(1)(h) — such additional documents, statements or records as will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information and evidence in paragraphs (a) to (g)`

§§ `Regulation 68(1) -- what an applicant must supply about a claimed disability`

-- src:666 | 68 (1) Where an applicant claims that he or some other person is disabled within the meaning of the Act, he shall supply the Minister with the following information in respect of the person whose disability is to be determined:
-- src:667 | (a) a report of any physical or mental disability including
-- src:668 | (i) the nature, extent and prognosis of the disability,
-- src:669 | (ii) the findings upon which the diagnosis and prognosis were made,
-- src:670 | (iii) any limitation resulting from the disability, and
-- src:671 | (iv) any other pertinent information, including recommendations for further diagnostic work or treatment, that may be relevant;
-- src:672 | (b) a statement of that person’s occupation and earnings for the period commencing on the date upon which the applicant alleges that the disability commenced; and
-- src:673 | (c) a statement of that person’s education, employment experience and activities of daily life.
@ref Reg 68(1) (src:666-673)
DECLARE `cr2 Item of information on a claimed disability under regulation 68(1)` IS ONE OF
    `reg 68(1)(a)(i) — a report of the nature, extent and prognosis of the disability`
    `reg 68(1)(a)(ii) — a report of the findings upon which the diagnosis and prognosis were made`
    `reg 68(1)(a)(iii) — a report of any limitation resulting from the disability`
    `reg 68(1)(a)(iv) — a report of any other pertinent information, including recommendations for further diagnostic work or treatment`
    `reg 68(1)(b) — a statement of the person's occupation and earnings for the period commencing on the date the applicant alleges the disability commenced`
    `reg 68(1)(c) — a statement of the person's education, employment experience and activities of daily life`

§§ `Regulation 72(2) -- what a request for reinstatement of a disability pension must be accompanied by`

-- src:710 | (2) The applicant or the person making a request on the applicant’s behalf shall furnish the Minister with the following information and evidence:
-- src:711 | (a) the applicant’s name, address and Social Insurance Number and, if applicable, the name and address of the person making the request on the applicant’s behalf and that person’s relationship to the applicant;
-- src:712 | (b) the month in which the applicant ceased to receive the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit;
-- src:713 | (c) the month in which the applicant became incapable again of working;
-- src:714 | (d) the date that the applicant stopped working;
-- src:715 | (e) the statement of a person qualified to practise medicine confirming that the applicant has a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability that is the same as, or is related to, the disability that entitled the applicant to receive the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit that is the subject of the request;
-- src:716 | (f) the name of each dependent child of the applicant and whether they are a child in respect of whom, either legally or in fact, the applicant has at least 20% of the parenting time; and
-- src:717 | (g) if the request includes a request to reinstate the disabled contributor’s child benefit in respect of each of the applicant’s children who are 18 years of age or more,
-- src:718 | (i) the child’s name, address and Social Insurance Number, and
-- src:719 | (ii) evidence, established in accordance with section 67, that the child is in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university.
@ref Reg 72(2) (src:710-719)
DECLARE `cr2 Item of information on a request for reinstatement under regulation 72(2)` IS ONE OF
    `reg 72(2)(a) — the applicant's name, address and Social Insurance Number and, if applicable, the name and address of the person making the request for the applicant and that person's relationship to the applicant`
    `reg 72(2)(b) — the month in which the applicant ceased to receive the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit`
    `reg 72(2)(c) — the month in which the applicant became incapable again of working`
    `reg 72(2)(d) — the date that the applicant stopped working`
    `reg 72(2)(e) — the statement of a person qualified to practise medicine confirming a severe and prolonged disability that is the same as, or related to, the disability that entitled the applicant to the pension or benefit`
    `reg 72(2)(f) — the name of each dependent child of the applicant and whether the applicant has at least 20% of the parenting time in respect of the child`
    `reg 72(2)(g)(i) — for each child aged 18 or more whose disabled contributor's child benefit is to be reinstated, the child's name, address and Social Insurance Number`
    `reg 72(2)(g)(ii) — for each such child, evidence, established in accordance with section 67, of full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university`

§§ `Regulation 74.1(1) -- what a request for reconsideration must set out`

-- src:726 | 74.1 (1) A request for a reconsideration under subsection 81(1) or (1.1) of the Act shall be made in writing to the Minister and shall set out
-- src:727 | (a) the name, address and Social Insurance Number of the contributor;
-- src:728 | (b) if the person making the request for the reconsideration is not the contributor, that person’s name and address and their relationship to the contributor; and
-- src:729 | (c) the grounds for the request for the reconsideration and a statement of the facts that form the basis of that request.
@ref Reg 74.1(1) (src:726-729)
DECLARE `cr2 Item of a request for reconsideration under regulation 74.1(1)` IS ONE OF
    `reg 74.1(1)(a) — the name, address and Social Insurance Number of the contributor`
    `reg 74.1(1)(b) — where the person making the request is not the contributor, that person's name and address and relationship to the contributor`
    `reg 74.1(1)(c) — the grounds for the request and a statement of the facts that form the basis of it`

§§ `Regulations 66 and 67 -- attendance at a school or university`

-- src:654 | 66 (1) For the purposes of paragraph (b) of the definition dependent child in subsection 42(1) of the Act,
-- src:655 | (a) full-time attendance at a school or university, with respect to a child, means that the child attends an educational institution that provides training or instruction of an educational, professional, vocational or technical nature and is enrolled in courses that constitute a course load recognized by the educational institution as full-time study; and
-- src:656 | (b) part-time attendance at a school or university, with respect to a child, means that the child, without being in full-time attendance at a school or university, attends an educational institution that provides training or instruction of an educational, professional, vocational or technical nature and is enrolled in courses that constitute at least 20 per cent of a course load recognized by the educational institution as constituting a full course load.
-- src:657 | (2) A child referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) who is absent from the educational institution during any normal period of scholastic vacation is considered to be in full-time or part-time attendance, as the case may be, at the educational institution during that period.
-- src:658 | (3) A child referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) who is absent from the educational institution because of illness is, during the period of that absence, considered to be in full-time attendance or part-time attendance, as the case may be, at the educational institution if
-- src:659 | (a) immediately after that absence and during the same academic year, the child resumes full-time or part-time attendance at any educational institution; or
-- src:660 | (b) in the case where the Minister has determined that the child is unable to comply with paragraph (a), the child resumes full-time or part-time attendance at any educational institution in the following academic year.
-- src:661 | (4) A child referred to in paragraph (3)(b) is considered to be in full-time attendance or part-time attendance, as the case may be, at the educational institution until the end of the normal period of scholastic vacation that follows the academic year in respect of which the child was determined by the Minister to be unable to resume attendance.
-- src:662 | (5) A child referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) who is absent from the educational institution because of illness and who, during this absence, dies or ceases to be a dependent child or disabled contributor’s child is considered to have been in full-time or part-time attendance, as the case may be, at the educational institution until the end of the month in which they die or in which they cease to be a dependent child or disabled contributor’s child.
@ref Reg 66 (src:654-662)
DECLARE `cr2 Attendance at a school or university` IS ONE OF
    `full-time attendance at a school or university`
    `part-time attendance at a school or university`
    `no attendance at a school or university`

@ref Reg 66(2), (3) (src:657-658)
DECLARE `cr2 Reason a child is absent from the educational institution` IS ONE OF
    `the child is not absent`
    `the child is absent during a normal period of scholastic vacation`
    `the child is absent because of illness`
    `the child is absent for some other reason`

§§ `Regulation 57 -- who may be paid a benefit unpaid at death`

-- src:597 | 57 A benefit payment may be paid to the estate of a deceased beneficiary, or if there is no estate, to a person or agency designated by the Minister, where
-- src:598 | (a) an amount is payable as a benefit to the deceased beneficiary; or
-- src:599 | (b) a benefit payment made to the beneficiary or made on behalf of the beneficiary by cheque or otherwise is returned to the Minister after the beneficiary’s death.
@ref Reg 57 (src:597-599)
DECLARE `cr2 Payee of a benefit payment unpaid at death` IS ONE OF
    `the estate of the deceased beneficiary`
    `a person or agency designated by the Minister`
    `nobody under regulation 57`

§§ `Regulation 64 -- who may be paid a death benefit when the estate does not claim it`

-- src:638 | 64 (1) If paragraph 71(2)(a) of the Act applies or the estate of a deceased contributor has not applied for the death benefit within 60 days after the contributor’s death, or if the amount of the death benefit is less than two thirds of 10% of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died, in the case of a death that occurred before January 1, 1998, or less than $2,387, in the case of a death that occurred after December 31, 1997 and before January 1, 2019, a direction under subsection 71(2) of the Act may, subject to subsections (2) and (3), be given for payment of the death benefit
-- src:639 | (a) to the individual or institution who has paid or is responsible for the payment of the deceased contributor’s funeral expenses;
-- src:640 | (b) in the absence of an individual or institution described in paragraph (a), to the survivor of the deceased contributor; or
-- src:641 | (c) in the absence of an individual or institution referred to in paragraph (a) and a survivor referred to in paragraph (b), to the next of kin of the deceased contributor.
-- src:642 | (2) No amount in excess of the actual funeral expenses shall be paid pursuant to paragraph (1)(a).
-- src:643 | (3) Where, by virtue of subsection (2), an amount paid pursuant to paragraph (1)(a) is less than the amount of the death benefit, a direction pursuant to subsection (1), in so far as it relates to the remainder of the death benefit, may be given as if in the absence of an individual or institution described in that paragraph.
@ref Reg 64 (src:638-643)
DECLARE `cr2 Payee of a death benefit other than the estate` IS ONE OF
    `the individual or institution that paid or is responsible for the payment of the funeral expenses`
    `the survivor of the deceased contributor`
    `the next of kin of the deceased contributor`
    `nobody under regulation 64`

§§ `Regulation 78.1(1)(c) -- a separation of one year or more followed by a resumption of cohabitation`

-- src:794 | (c) where, after having lived separate and apart for one year or more, the persons subject to the division resumed cohabitation for at least one year, the period of that separation shall be considered to have begun with the first month of the year in which they commenced to live separate and apart and to have ended with the last month of the year immediately preceding the year in which they resumed cohabitation.
@ref Reg 78.1(1)(c) (src:794)
DECLARE `cr2 Separation followed by resumed cohabitation` HAS
    `the date they commenced to live separate and apart` IS A DATE
    `they lived separate and apart for one year or more` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date they resumed cohabitation` IS A DATE
    `they resumed cohabitation for at least one year` IS A BOOLEAN
